course: dictionary
lesson: 15229
title: Fair and unfair words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell us when people are treated unfairly. Sexist is one of them. It describes words or behaviour that treat someone badly just because they are a boy or a girl, a man or a woman. Look at the clues in the sentence. «The coach said girls should not play football.» The words girls and should not show the unfair idea, so this is a sexist comment.
explain: Sexist can also be a noun, meaning a person who thinks or behaves in this unfair way. «He is a sexist, because he says boys can't cry.» Here the word tells us about the person. Remember that anyone can say or do sexist things, not only men or boys.
explain: A good check is to swap in a different group and see if the idea is still unfair. «Boys can't cook» is sexist, because it judges every boy by his sex. «Some people enjoy cooking» is fair, because it talks about people, not about what their sex should be able to do.
fact: Sexist is an adjective and a noun: a sexist joke, or a sexist person.
fact: «Sexist» means treating people unfairly or badly because they are a boy or a girl, a man or a woman.
fact: «Sexist» can describe a comment, a joke, an advert or a rule.
fact: Schools teach that everyone should have the same chances, whatever their sex.
fact: Phrases you may hear: «sexist comment», «sexist joke», «That's sexist.»
exercise: «Girls can't play football.» What makes this sentence sexist? | It is about football | It is a question | *It judges all girls unfairly because they are girls | It is very loud
exercise: Ben says, «That's sexist!» after a joke. What does sexist mean? | *Unfair to people because they are a boy or a girl | Very old | Very funny | Very quiet
exercise: Which phrase is a sexist comment? | «It's sunny today.» | «Well done on your painting.» | *«Boys can't cry.» | «Let's read a book.»
test: Why is «Only girls can be nurses» sexist? | It describes a colour | It is a question | It is a true fact about hospitals | *It treats people unfairly because of their sex
test: What is a sexist? | A person who writes stories | A person who loves football | A teacher who marks work | *A person who treats people unfairly because they are a boy or a girl
exam: Which sentence is NOT sexist? | «Girls can't be doctors.» | «Only men can fix cars.» | *«Anyone can be a good doctor, whatever their sex.» | «Boys don't do ballet.»
